t do not happen  and it will be completely unreasonable  to claim that the first episode of  shield hero is actively encouraging all  men to see all women as evil and  conniving this is the same logic that  claims that violent video games  encourage violence in real life it  implies that the viewers who watch the  anime and see this one evil female  character doing evil things will begin  to see all women in general as evil and  deceitful it is worth noting than in  shield hero there are far more male  characters who are shown in a negative  light than female characters including  the spear hero who is incredibly  gullible and full of himself the King  who plots against an innocent man the  men who insult and try to rob the shield  hero in the streets the male slave  trader and  many more the fact that one villainous  female character did something  villainous to a fictional male character  in an anime obviously does not mean that  all women are villains in the real world  both women and men have the potential to  be good people and a potential to be bad  people this is simply human nature and  the claim that one evil female character  who does evil things is representative  of the author's overall outlook on women  is both intellectually dishonest and  malicious this unfounded claim willfully  slanders the character and reputation of  the author despite the fact that next to  nothing is actually known about the  author can you imagine anything more  intellectually dishonest and malicious  than trying to slander and ruin the  reputation of someone you know next to  nothing about but with all of that said  I personally feel that the first episode  of shield hero was one of the weaker  episodes so far I say this because the  motivations of the spear hero the female  villain mine and the king are kind of  weak in my opinion this fantasy world is  facing an existential threat that only  the four legendary heroes can stop so  why in the world would the king and  other members of this kingdom conspire  to destroy one of the legendary heroes  thereby decreasing their own chances of  survival why would the spear hero be so  ready to believe every horrible thing  that he hears about the shield hero when  they were both just sent into this  unknown world together and it is logical  to assume that working together for a  common purpose would increase their  chances of actually surviving why in the  world did mine blatantly steal the  shield heroes silver coins and items if  she was presenting herself to be the  victim in the situation I did not get  the impression that these items were  exceptionally rare or hard to obtain  especially for the four legendary heroes  now it is true that the shield hero has  the reputation of being the weakest but  even with that in mind it has been  prophesized that only these four  legendary heroes can save mankind there  are four of them for a reason so the  idea that the king and the others were  under threat of total destruction would  decide to simply do away with one of the  legendary heroes who  surely did nothing wrong to any of them  doesn't make much sense to me  there could be an explanation for all of  this later on in the story in which case  I look forward to seeing it but these  were just my thoughts in terms of the  first episode itself however once the  betrayal happens and the shield hero is  cast out to wander the kingdom on his  own this story does become extremely  interesting and the message it conveys  is powerful the shield hero was summoned  into this fantasy world through no fault  of his own he was never given a choice  and then instead of being respected and  adorned he was betrayed shunned and  mocked at this point he does become  angry and jaded and he decides that the  only way to survive is to be hard on the  world that has been so hard on him he  forces merchants to be fair to him  instead of ripping him off with the  threat of violence he doesn't hesitate  to use underhanded tactics to protect  himself from potential attack and after  he realizes that he cannot gain  experience in advance as a hero without  someone handling the offensive element  of battles he decides to purchase a  slave to do the attacking for him some  critics of the anime have accused it of  literally promoting slavery because of  this event in the story but in the  fantasy world in which the shield hero  was forced to come against his will  enslaving deme humans who are part human  and part animal is considered completely  acceptable at least by a large segment  of the population now who me the shield  hero after being framed robbed and  shunned by everyone in a dangerous and  unfamiliar world decides that the only  way to survive in this world is to play  by the rules of that world he decides to  do whatever it takes to survive even if  that means giving the inhabitants of  that world a taste of their own bitter  medicine however as soon as the shield  hero buys a sickly demi-human girl  called ruff Talia he instantly feels  compassion towards her in spite of  himself he goes out of his way to cure  her illness and to comfort her as she  deals with tragic flashbacks of losing  her parents and being forced into  slavery despite the fact that he may be  better off just being cruel to others as  they had been cruel to him the shield  hero cannot help but feel compassion for  ruff Talia he mentors her helps her grow  and develop as both a fighter and a  person and he goes out of his way  to make her happy when he is later  accused of enslaving and mistreating  raff Thalia by the spear hero ruff  Thalia defends the shield hero because  she has come to both trust him and care  for him and just a side note isn't it  ironic that this anime is being accused  of promoting sexism when the main  character literally has a woman fighting  his battles for him  a woman who also happens to be a great  character someone who is brave kind and  has impressive combat skills it is clear  to me personally that the rising of the  shield hero is not a story about hate or  anger  if you bother to give the show more than  a few minutes of your time you quickly  realize that the true message of shield  hero is the importance of being brave in  the face of extremely difficult odds and  the undeniable power of basic human  compassion no amount of hate lies and  mockery could make now for me the shield  hero hateful and jaded enough to numb  his natural sense of compassion for a  fellow human being despite the fact that  ruff Thalia is labeled a slave and  despite the fact that she is considered  to be less than human in this particular  society the shield hero cannot bring  himself to treat her poorly even though  he was made to suffer by others he can't  bring himself to just take his  frustrations out on another innocent  person the message that I got from the  rising of the shield hero is this  sometimes in life we come across bad  people these bad people can be male or  female and because of these bad people  we may find ourselves facing extremely  difficult odds but even if we find  ourselves in such an unfortunate  situation we cannot and must not forget  the importance of compassion we cannot  allow ourselves to succumb to injustice  and we must not allow ourselves to  become as bad as the people who  mistreated us we have to be brave  stubborn clever and we have to persevere  and we always have to remember that even  with all the evil in the world there are  also many good people out there innocent  people who might also be suffering and  struggling we cannot allow ourselves to  become so jaded that we would mistreat  these innocent people in the same way  that we were mistreated by others and  just like the shield hero every rational  person knows that enslaving another  human being  is wrong even if they look different  than we do or have a different social  status than we do  our basic sense of empathy and  compassion for our fellow human beings  will lead us to the truth and just like  the shield hero we must listen to our  heart and do the right thing even if  that same level of compassion was not  granted to us by others life is not  always fair and we will not always be  treated fairly by others and yeah that  sucks  but this does not mean that we should  give up and become as bad as the people  who have treated us badly on the  contrary we should stubbornly fight  against injustice and we should treat  others with compassion even when we are  told that these others are allegedly  different from us or beneath us socially  this in my opinion is the true message  of the shield hero anime thus far and  all those individuals who jumped to  judge this series and even the author of  the series based on their own biased  interpretation of the first episode have  said more about themselves than I could  ever say here they have demonstrated the  same willfully ignorant and intolerant  behavior that the villains of the story  have demonstrated towards the shield  hero and it is nothing short of poetic  justice that the shield hero's  perseverance and compassion against all  odds is winning over so many anime fans  across the world while those who  unfairly criticized the shield hero both  the character and the series have been  repudiated by the wider anime community  if you enjoyed this video and you want  to see more videos like it you can leave  a like to let me know if you're new to  anime uproar don't forget to subscribe  and hit that notification valve if you  want to talk more about the shield hero  or maybe you have some ideas for future  videos feel free to hit me up on Twitter  and Instagram at anime uproar and  finally I want to say a big thank you to  everyone who has been supporting anime  up or on patreon both now and in the  past if you want to support more content  on this channel feel free to check out  our patreon page linked in the  description as always thank you guys so  much for watching and until next time  see you space cowboys  [Music]  you  [Music]

